  "per_rule_foe": {},
  "scope": "Same frozen prefix state, candidate first decision only. Served Native depth-2 actor-perspective score in native units; terminal band pairs excluded from means and counted. Post-hoc secondary observable, not W-L and not a preregistered endpoint. Coverage is limited to cells where the candidate profile actually moved first: the Unit-vs-uniform owner-0 game is the only paid uniform cell, so the uniform foe cells contain owner-0 candidate pairs only, while both-owner cells exist for the fixed-random foes. The served first-decision score is foe-independent, so the owner-0 cells are identical across foes; only the owner split adds information. However the owner split is confounded with ply and decision state: every scorable owner-0 pair is at relative ply 0 and every owner-1 pair at ply 1, and no (rule, family) shares the candidate's first-decision state across owners (0/182 free, 0/92 classic), although 576/576 free and 3456/3456 classic both-owner game groups start from the same frozen game root. The role cells are therefore not a matched replication."
 },
